  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO supports the Jamaica Confederation of Trade Unions (JCTU) and affiliated unions by strengthening their capacity to influence policymaking on climate and labour justice. This support includes technical assistance to develop a position paper on the impact of Just Transition on workers in Jamaica and to produce trade union proposals for the integration of labour concerns into the country&#x2019;s updated Nationally Determined Contributions (NDCs) and broader social dialogue frameworks. Awareness-raising workshops will be held with national and second-level union leaders, along with the development of targeted communication materials, such as a brochure for domestic workers. In collaboration with JCTU and Jamaica Household Workers&apos; Union (JHWU), the ILO will also provide technical support to formulate proposals for inclusive social protection and design an assessment tool to evaluate the impact of extreme weather events, such as Hurricane Beryl, on domestic workers. These interventions aim to ensure trade union perspectives are meaningfully reflected in Jamaica&#x2019;s climate policies and labour protection strategies.</narrative>
  </description>
